Falsifies `capability::from_bits_cannot_forge_a_right`.

The defect: the mask dropped from `Rights::from_bits`, `Rights(bits)` instead of
`Rights(bits & Rights::ALL.0)`. `from_bits` takes an attacker-controlled syscall
register, so this is the exact shape of a real hole: userspace hands the kernel a u32 and
the kernel believes all 32 bits of it.

Expected to fail: `assert!(Rights::from_bits(raw).is_subset_of(Rights::ALL))`, on any
`raw` with a bit above bit 3 set.

diff --git a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
index d65bed7d..f33c0989 100644
--- a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@ impl Rights {
     /// [`bits`](Self::bits), for rights that crossed a boundary in a syscall register. Undefined
     /// bits are dropped, so a caller cannot conjure a right that does not exist.
     pub const fn from_bits(bits: u32) -> Rights {
-        Rights(bits & Rights::ALL.0)
+        Rights(bits)
     }
 
     /// Every right either side holds.
